341 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(WHO REALLY PROFITS FROM FASHION?)/Pg 27 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(There is an appealing logic to making millions of variations on the same T-shirt. Buy in bulk, work with established factories and spread development costs over enormous production runs. Surely the margins should follow?)/Pg 27 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(Not necessarily. Inditex led in every year over those five years, Fast Retailings margin improved from 50.3% to 53.8%; Inditexs rose from 57.1% to 58.3%.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(That does not make UNIQLOs scale irrelevant. Savings may help keep prices accessible rather than appear entirely as higher margins. Inditexs edge may reflect pricing, product mix, sourcing or markdown outcomes. The accounts show who earned more from each sale„not which single decision caused it.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(One model promises purchasing power; the other, responsiveness. Yet the income statements tell a less predictable story.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(The Scale Advantage That Wasnt)/Pg 27 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(Gross margin is only the first stop. Stores, staff, logistics and technology all take their share before revenue becomes operating profit.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(For every 100 units of FY2025 revenue, Fast Retailing spent 46.22 on cost of sales and another 37.19 in net operating charges, leaving 16.59 in operating profit. Inditex spent 41.75 and 38.19 respectively, leaving 20.06. Its 4.47-point gross-margin lead narrowed to 3.47 points at the operating level.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 129 0 R/E(There is an accounting wrinkle: Fast Retailing includes depreciation and amortisation within SG&A, while Inditex reports them separately. The net operating charges shown here are an analyst-defined residual„gross profit less operating profit„not a like-for-like SG&A measure.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj
