370 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(Fashion's global ambitions come with a shopping list of their own: new markets, smarter stores, better technology. Each promises tomorrow's customers. None comes free today.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(In FY2025, Fast Retailing sold 9.6% more, taking revenue to ¥3.40 trillion. Inditex grew 3.2% to  39.86 billion. A good year for the shop windows, then. Less so for the cash-flow statements: Fast Retailing's operating cash fell from ¥651.5 billion to ¥580.6 billion, while Inditex slipped from  9.29 billion to  9.23 billion.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(THE SALES ARE UP. SO WHERE'S THE CASH?)/Pg 30 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 132 0 R/E(At Fast Retailing, the contrast was especially sharp: revenue up almost a tenth, operating cash down 10.9%. The top line was moving in one direction; the money coming in from operations was moving in another. Growth, evidently, is not a cash machine.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj
374 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 132 0 R/Pg 30 0 R/A[702 0 R 0]/K[4]>>
endobj
