endobj
405 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(TWO FASHION GIANTS. ONE SHOPPING DISTRICT. )/Pg 35 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(AND A FEW SURPRISES BETWEEN THE RACKS.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(ON SINGAPORE'S ORCHARD ROAD, UNIQLO AND ZARA SELL DIFFERENT IDEAS OF WHAT A WARDROBE SHOULD BE. AFTER FIVE YEARS IN THE ACCOUNTS, WE WENT TO THEIR STORES TO SEE HOW THOSE IDEAS HOLD UP IN THE REAL WORLD.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(Orchard Road has no shortage of brands competing for attention. Among its best-known addresses are UNIQLO's Orchard Central Global Flagship Store and Zara at ION Orchard: two prominent stores in Singapore's premier shopping district, each making a very different promise to customers.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj
409 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(We sampled 30 apparel styles at each location, looked for markdowns and examined the services surrounding the clothes. The aim was to find out what a business model looks like once it reaches a hanger.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(BACK TO)/Pg 35 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj
411 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(THE STORE)/Pg 35 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj
412 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(WHERE THE STRATEGY MEETS THE SHOP FLOOR)/Pg 35 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj
413 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(A QUESTION OF COLOUR)/Pg 35 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj
414 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(At UNIQLO, even a familiar sweater can come with a surprisingly long decision over colour. Our sampled styles averaged 4.73 recorded colour options apiece, against 2.53 at Zara. One UNIQLO cashmere crew-neck sweater alone offered 14.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj
415 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 137 0 R/E(Zara's racks made a different pitch. The interest was more often in a particular cut or silhouette than in another shade of the same piece. Of our 30 sampled styles, 24 at UNIQLO were classified as basic or functional; at Zara, 18 were. Neither shop fitted its stereotype perfectly. Zara had basics, and UNIQLO had design-led pieces too. But the contrast suggested two ways to offer choice: variations on the familiar, or more reasons to try something new.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj
416 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 137 0 R/Pg 35 0 R/A[712 0 R 0]/K[13]>>
endobj
417 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 138 0 R/Pg 36 0 R/A[713 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 138 0 R/Pg 36 0 R/A[714 0 R 0]/K[1]>>
endobj
419 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 138 0 R/Pg 36 0 R/A[715 0 R 0]/K[2]>>
endobj
420 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 138 0 R/E(Two prominent stores and 60 sampled garments cannot explain five years of group-level margins or inventory turnover. But UNIQLO's colour depth gave LifeWear a tangible form; Zara's assortment made the appeal of discovery easier to see. The vanished sale tags exposed the importance of timing, while shared checkout technology showed how much these supposed opposites have in common.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj
421 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 138 0 R/E(Scale and speed make a good headline. On Orchard Road, the businesses behind those words looked more interesting„and less tidy.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 138 0 R/E(THE MISSING SALE TAGS)/Pg 36 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 138 0 R/E(The discount racks supplied the day's best twist. At UNIQLO we deliberately recorded ten reduced-price styles, marked down by roughly 17% to 50%. At Zara we found none. For a brand famous for fast-moving fashion, the empty discount trail was intriguing.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj
424 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 138 0 R/E(Then a Zara employee explained that the annual Black Friday promotional season had not yet begun. Suddenly the apparent difference in promotional behaviour looked rather more like a difference in timing.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj
425 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 138 0 R/E(That exchange mattered more than a neat comparison chart would have. Our UNIQLO markdown sample was selected from discounted products; there was no equivalent Zara sample that day. It says nothing reliable about either chain's annual discount frequency. And, as our earlier accounting feature showed, a sale tag is not automatically an inventory write-down. Sometimes the most useful discovery is why an observation cannot bear the weight of a bigger claim.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj
426 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 138 0 R/E(BEYOND THE CLOTHES)/Pg 36 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 138 0 R/E(Both stores had self-checkout facilities: our notes counted 11 stations at each. Convenience, it seems, is no longer a contest with only one entrant. The differences were in the experience around the machines.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj
