443 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(On Singapore's Orchard Road, two shopping bags can tell two very different stories. The clothes look different, so do the businesses behind them. UNIQLO has built its appeal on improving the everyday; Zara on keeping pace with what comes next. It makes for a tidy rivalry: scale versus speed. Five years of accounts, and a visit to the shop floor, have made that rivalry rather less tidy.)/Pg 37 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj
444 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(A LEADER, NOT A SIMPLE EXPLANATION)/Pg 37 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj
445 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(If the scoreboard alone settled the argument, Inditex would have the stronger claim. From FY2021 to FY2025, the group behind Zara turned inventory faster and reported higher gross and operating margins than Fast Retailing. In FY2025, it also generated more sales per unit of average assets and retained a larger share of revenue after selected capital investment and lease payments.)/Pg 37 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj
446 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(For a business associated with constantly changing collections, that is a striking combination. Fashion's quick tempo has not prevented strong reported margins or stock discipline.)/Pg 37 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj
447 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(But Fast Retailing has not been standing still. After FY2022's inventory difficulties, it improved stock turnover; in FY2025, its operating margin rose even as its gross margin edged down. The business of everyday clothing has been learning, too.)/Pg 37 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj
448 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 139 0 R/E(There is a financial leader here. What the accounts cannot isolate is how much of the lead comes from speed itself, rather than pricing, product mix, geography or the other brands inside each group.)/Pg 37 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj
449 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(Scale builds reach. Speed creates relevance. But discipline is what gives either one staying power.Ž)/Pg 38 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj
450 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(WHAT THE STORES ADDED)/Pg 38 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj
451 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(Orchard Road supplied a useful counterpoint to the spreadsheets. At UNIQLO's Orchard Central Global Flagship Store, our sampled garments offered a deeper range of colours. At Zara's ION Orchard store, the sample leaned more towards distinctive designs. The differences were visible, but neither shop fitted its label perfectly.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj
452 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(The most revealing moment was almost a non-event: no sale tags at Zara during our visit because the sale season hadn't started yet. Suddenly a seemingly telling contrast became a reminder of how much timing shapes an observation.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj
453 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E( Convenience was common ground for both stores. The visits could not explain group margins or cash flows. They did show how much more complicated the businesses are than their shorthand descriptions.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj
454 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(THE CONTEST THAT MATTERS)/Pg 38 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj
455 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(For UNIQLO, the challenge is to keep familiar products useful and desirable across new markets without allowing scale to become excess stock. For Zara, it is to keep fashion responsive without letting the machinery of responsiveness consume the value it creates.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj
456 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(Both must make decisions before a customer ever reaches the fitting room: what to make, how much to order, when to change course and where to invest. A full shop is not necessarily a profitable one. Growing sales do not guarantee growing cash. And a new flagship store brings bills long after its opening day.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj
457 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(So who wins? On the measures examined, Inditex has the stronger group-level financial record. That judgment should not be softened into a diplomatic draw. Nor should it be mistaken for proof that Zara's strategy would outperform UNIQLO's under identical conditions.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj
458 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 140 0 R/E(What lasts is not a formula for producing more, or a talent for changing faster. It is the discipline to know when each is worth doing.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj
459 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 140 0 R/Pg 38 0 R/A[722 0 R 0]/K[10]>>
endobj
460 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 140 0 R/Pg 38 0 R/A[723 0 R 0]/K[11]>>
endobj
461 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 140 0 R/Pg 38 0 R/A[724 0 R 0]/K[12]>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 140 0 R/Pg 38 0 R/A[725 0 R 0]/K[13]>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 141 0 R/Pg 39 0 R/A[726 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 141 0 R/E(BEHIND THE NUMBERS)/Pg 39 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 141 0 R/E(A short guide to the evidence behind this issue.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 141 0 R/E(Behind the fashion story sit annual reports, calculation workbooks and original store observations. Here is how we read them.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj
467 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 141 0 R/Pg 39 0 R/A[727 0 R 0]/K[4]>>
endobj
468 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 141 0 R/Pg 39 0 R/A[728 0 R 0]/K[5]>>
endobj
469 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 142 0 R/E(Our principal comparison uses each groups FY2021…FY2025 consolidated accounts. Fast Retailing closes on 31 August; Inditex closes on 31 January of the following calendar year. We retain yen and euros in their original reporting currencies, and compare ratios calculated within each group rather than unconverted cash amounts.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj
470 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 142 0 R/E(At UNIQLO Orchard Central Global Flagship Store and Zara ION Orchard, we sampled 30 apparel styles per retailer and observed discounts, services and customer-facing technology. The selections were exploratory, not statistically representative. Some colour-option records may include online availability. The observation cannot establish annual discount frequency.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 142 0 R/E(Inventory turnover uses cost of sales divided by average inventory; days inventory outstanding is 365 divided by turnover. Under IAS 2, inventory is measured at the lower of cost and NRV. Fast Retailings write-down expenses and Inditexs changes in provisions are different disclosures. Expense classifications also differ, particularly for depreciation and amortisation.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj
472 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 142 0 R/E(P4 explains why the parent groups are useful financial lenses for these flagship brands. Here, the rule is narrower: group accounts do not isolate brand-only margins, and a store visit cannot prove what caused a five-year financial difference. Our interpretations distinguish reported outcomes from possible business explanations.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj
473 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 142 0 R/E(Our post-lease cashŽ measure subtracts cash purchases of property, plant and equipment, intangible assets and selected financing lease cash payments from operating cash flow. It is an editorial analytical measure, not an IFRS subtotal. The lease cash-flow captions are not perfectly harmonised between the two issuers.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj
474 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 142 0 R/E(Primary sources: Fast Retailing and Inditex FY2021…FY2025 annual reports and accompanying notes; the teams financial calculation workbooks; and original Orchard Road field records. P4s FY2025 brand-related revenue shares were checked against the issuers annual reports. The Inditex figure combines Zara, Zara Home and Lefties„not Zara alone.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj
